      "description": "Rail cells: resting, current (ink) and cited (maroon border).",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-cells\"><button class=\"ds-cell\">5</button><button class=\"ds-cell ds-cell--cited\">6</button><button class=\"ds-cell ds-cell--current\">8</button><button class=\"ds-cell\">9</button></div>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#faf8f3;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#1c1b19;--ink-2:#45433e;--ink-3:#6b675f;--rule:#dedad0;--rule-strong:#b5b0a4;--maroon:#7a1f1f;--maroon-deep:#641818;--maroon-wash:#f4e8e4;--maroon-line:#d9b9b2;--sans:'Hind','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;--serif:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}.ds-cells{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,38px);gap:4px}.ds-cell{height:36px;border:1px solid var(--rule);background:#fff;border-radius:0;font:500 15px var(--sans);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}.ds-cell:hover{border-color:var(--ink)}.ds-cell--current{background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);color:#fff}.ds-cell--cited{border:2px solid var(--maroon);color:var(--maroon-deep);font-weight:700}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Citation Chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip-citation",
      "description": "Jump to another cited clause or sub-section.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-cite-chip\">also Section 8(6)</button>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#faf8f3;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#1c1b19;--ink-2:#45433e;--ink-3:#6b675f;--rule:#dedad0;--rule-strong:#b5b0a4;--maroon:#7a1f1f;--maroon-deep:#641818;--maroon-wash:#f4e8e4;--maroon-line:#d9b9b2;--sans:'Hind','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;--serif:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}.ds-cite-chip{height:30px;padding:0 10px;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong);background:#fff;border-radius:0;font:14.5px var(--sans);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}.ds-cite-chip:hover{border-color:var(--ink)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Side-by-side Pair",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "law-column",
      "description": "Plain words beside the Act's verbatim text, with modality underlines.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pair\"><div><h4>In plain words</h4><p>You <u class=\"may\">can</u> withdraw your consent whenever you want.</p></div><div class=\"law\"><h4>The Act says</h4><p>(4) Where consent given by the Data Principal is the basis of processing of personal data, such Data Principal <u class=\"duty\">shall</u> have the right to withdraw her consent at any time.</p></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#faf8f3;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#1c1b19;--ink-2:#45433e;--ink-3:#6b675f;--rule:#dedad0;--rule-strong:#b5b0a4;--maroon:#7a1f1f;--maroon-deep:#641818;--maroon-wash:#f4e8e4;--maroon-line:#d9b9b2;--sans:'Hind','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;--serif:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}.ds-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong)}.ds-pair>div{padding:24px 32px}.ds-pair .law{background:var(--paper);border-left:1px solid var(--rule-strong)}.ds-pair h4{margin:0 0 12px;font:700 15px var(--sans)}.ds-pair p{margin:0;font:18px/1.6 var(--sans)}.ds-pair .law p{font:16px/1.65 var(--serif)}.ds-pair u{text-decoration-color:var(--maroon);text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px}.ds-pair u.may{text-decoration-style:dashed}.ds-pair u:hover{background:var(--maroon-wash);color:var(--maroon-deep)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Result Headline",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "result-frame",
      "description": "Head field of a result: citation, title, chapter, timing.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-head\"><div><p class=\"c\">Section 8<small>(6)</small></p><p class=\"t\">General obligations of Data Fiduciary</p><p class=\"ch\">Chapter II · Obligations of Data Fiduciary</p></div><p class=\"m\">Answered in 5.8 s</p></div>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#faf8f3;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#1c1b19;--ink-2:#45433e;--ink-3:#6b675f;--rule:#dedad0;--rule-strong:#b5b0a4;--maroon:#7a1f1f;--maroon-deep:#641818;--maroon-wash:#f4e8e4;--maroon-line:#d9b9b2;--sans:'Hind','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;--serif:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}.ds-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;padding:32px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong)}.ds-head p{margin:0}.ds-head .c{font:600 32px/1.1 var(--serif)}.ds-head .c small{font-size:20px;font-weight:400;color:var(--ink-3)}.ds-head .t{font-size:18px;margin-top:8px}.ds-head .ch{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-3)}.ds-head .m{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-3);white-space:nowrap}"
    },
    {
      "name": "NOT COVERED Stamp",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "stamp-not-covered",
      "description": "Shown instead of an answer when the Act is silent.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-stamp\">Not covered<small>by the DPDP Act, 2023</small></p>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#faf8f3;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#1c1b19;--ink-2:#45433e;--ink-3:#6b675f;--rule:#dedad0;--rule-strong:#b5b0a4;--maroon:#7a1f1f;--maroon-deep:#641818;--maroon-wash:#f4e8e4;--maroon-line:#d9b9b2;--sans:'Hind','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;--serif:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}.ds-stamp{display:inline-block;margin:0;padding:10px 18px 8px;border:3px double var(--maroon);border-radius:2px;color:var(--maroon);font:700 26px/1.05 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;transform:rotate(-2deg)}.ds-stamp small{display:block;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.2em;font-weight:600;margin-top:4px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Printed Reference",
    "overview": "**North Star: \"The Printed Reference\"**\n\nThe page should look like something a careful person made for reading the law, not like a chat product. That means warm off-white paper, near-black ink, serif headings, thin rules between fields, square corners, and one dark maroon accent used for links and for marking. Nothing is decorative: there is no colour band, logo badge, pill, glow, gradient or entrance animation. Every element is either text the reader needs or a rule that separates it.\n\nThe core of the page is unchanged from the first version. Each result is one ruled frame whose headline is the citation (for example \"Section 8(6)\"). The plain-language rewrite and the Act's verbatim text sit side by side on one centre rule, with obligation words marked by underline form. When the Act does not cover a question the frame shows a NOT COVERED stamp instead of an answer.\n\nA 300px rail lists all 44 sections and the Schedule as numbered cells under chapter titles. The work column (up to 1180px) holds the question box and the result. Body text is 17px; nothing that carries meaning is smaller than 13px.\n\nThis version replaced an earlier purple design (violet header band, pill chips, guilloche line, monospaced serial numbers, fade-in animations) because it read as a generic AI-generated interface.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper ground (#faf8f3) and a white result sheet, separated by 1px rules, not shadows.",
      "Near-black ink for text, the primary button and the current section; dark maroon only for links, modality underlines, the cited section and the stamp.",
      "Noto Serif for headings and for the Act's own words; Hind for everything the tool itself says.",
      "Square or 2px corners throughout. No pills.",
      "Obligation force carried by underline form (solid, double, dashed), never by colour.",
      "No entrance animation. Only short colour and border transitions on hover."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink First Rule",
        "body": "Solid fills are ink, not accent: the Ask button and the current section cell are near-black. Maroon appears as text, underline or border, never as a large fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warm Paper Rule",
        "body": "Grounds are warm off-white (#faf8f3 family), never cool grey-lilac or pure white at page level. Pure white is reserved for the sheet things are printed on.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Noto Serif is for headings and the Act's words; Hind is for what the tool says. A serif sentence in body copy that is not the Act's text is a bug.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Citation Headline Rule",
        "body": "The largest type on any result is the section reference.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Not Shadow Rule",
